  <section class="sec" id="roads">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">The idea</p>
      <h2 class="reveal" style="--d:1">The same ten questions are <em>eating your day.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede reveal" style="--d:2;margin-top:24px">Fast replies win customers. But handing your inbox to an AI feels risky, and it should. So every email takes one of three roads.</p>
      <div class="roads">
        <article class="road reveal" style="--d:0"><span class="k">01 &middot; Routine</span><h3>Answered in minutes</h3><p>Delivery times, returns, opening hours, payment methods. Answered from your own Google Sheet, in your customer's language.</p><span class="tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12.5 4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg>Sent automatically</span></article>
        <article class="road hold reveal" style="--d:1"><span class="k">02 &middot; Risky</span><h3>Held for you</h3><p>Refunds, discounts, complaints, legal threats, angry customers. The AI writes a draft, but nothing is sent until you approve.</p><span class="tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5"/><path d="M12 7.5V12l3 2"/></svg>Waits for your approval</span></article>
        <article class="road reveal" style="--d:2"><span class="k">03 &middot; Unknown</span><h3>Handed to you</h3><p>If your sheet has no answer, the AI doesn't guess. The email lands in your queue and you write the reply.</p><span class="tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 20l4.5-1 10-10a2.1 2.1 0 0 0-3-3l-10 10z"/></svg>You write it</span></article>
      </div>
    </div>
